        "date": "2026-11-26T09:13:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Sinumerik 840D cutting-edge D and a rapid G53 retract\n\nThe 840D post wrote `T<n> D<n> M6`. D selects an offset data block of\nthe active tool (840D sl Fundamentals 12/2018, section 6.6), so tool 12\nselected an edge D12 that it does not have. The tool call now writes D1.\nA machine file can state `tooling.d_number: \"tool-number\"` for a control\nset to free D numbers with D equal to T.\n\nEach G53 Z retract (setup change, home ask, program end) is now\n`G0 G53 Z.. D0`. The program end had no G0, so it moved at the modal\nfeed or alarmed after G2/G3. G53 suppresses frames only (sections 9.1,\n13.10); D0 deselects the tool length (section 6.6), as the manual's own\nexample `G0 G53 X.. Z.. D0` does (section 4.4). A later section with the\nsame tool selects its D again before its first move.\n\nFixes #4143\nFixes #4144\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
